  "question": "Cross-encoder reranking is described as more accurate than bi-encoder cosine similarity because it lets query and document attend to each other directly \u2014 what does that accuracy improvement actually cost a pipeline in milliseconds when reranking a typical shortlist?",
  "answer": "Cross\u2011encoder reranking adds a noticeable latency penalty: when you rerank a typical shortlist of\u202f\u2248\u202f20\u202f\u2013\u202f50 candidates, the extra forward\u2011passes required by the cross\u2011encoder usually cost on the order of **100\u202fto\u202f300\u202fms** of additional latency\u3010latency-budgets-in-a-rag-pipeline::1\u3011. This is the concrete price of the accuracy gain that comes from letting the query and document attend to each other directly\u3010reranking-with-cross-encoders::1\u3011.",
